{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf","id":813506,"title":"Sell an Apocalypse fan on Forsaken; or W;tF=WTF?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-21T11:22:42-08:00","id":813506,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Sell an Apocalypse fan on Forsaken; or W;tF=WTF?","content":"My favorite game line of the CWoD was W:tA. I've been a fan of wolves and werewolves and werecreatures of all kinds for as long as I can remember. The moment I picked up W:tA Players Guide 2ed, I was hooked. A game with werewolves as the good guys? Against a palpable force of entropy and death? Fate of the world at stake? Sign me Up! So imagine my disappointment upon reading W:tF, and finding NOTHING that I could relate to. Tribes that had no connection to any existing culture or mythology. No global treat or conspiracy to struggle against. Gone were Gaia's defenders, replaced with the spiritual equivalent of a Border Patrol. WTF, indeed! So, aside from the sandbox ruleset,(still not sure that's a feature, I miss having Metaplot as a backdrop, you could always ignore it if it didn't fit your story) what's so great about Forsaken?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T12:07:22-08:00","id":813538,"title":"","content":"Well, the big draws for me are that Tribes are wholly unique and don't have any connection to existing culture or mythology, a lack of a global threat or conspiracy for werewolves to struggle against, that werewolves mostly stick to protecting their territories and there aren't Septs or large-scale hierarchies and aren't environmental activists, and that there's no major metaplot to color the players' ideas about the setting or distract from the activities of the PCs.<br /> <br /> So what I'm saying is that I'm probably not the best person to sell it to you.<br /> <br /> I've got some friends who prefer Apocalypse but have some nice things to say about Forsaken, I'll repeat what they say:<ul><li>The way the spirit world works in Forsaken is more interesting than in Apocalypse: They like that all spirits are Darwinian and alien and such, and that even spirits of &quot;good&quot; things can behave terribly.</li> <li>Werewolves aren't all necessarily defenders of Gaia, and they're not forced into the role of soldiers.</li> <li>If you want werewolf organizations bigger than packs that are based on real-world mythology or culture, there are Lodges which are nicely integrated.</li> </ul><br /> That's it.<br /> <br /> I like 2E Forsaken better than 1E. The emphasis on packs and territory management reminds me of Ars Magica. Wolf-Blooded got an expanded role and some more interesting build options to match. The <i>idigam</i> are probably the coolest enemies I've encountered in WoD or CofD because they're alien cosmic entities that are badass and can dramatically alter the tone and scope of your Chronicle, but won't derail the setting (for example, I'm running a game set in the 90s in Washington state and also a game set in 2015 Texas: the 90s werewolves can all be wiped out by an idigam, but the Texas ones won't necessarily be affected).<br /> <br /> Hope that helps, and I hope somebody else can help more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T12:17:57-08:00","id":813550,"title":"","content":"Forsaken is fun because it is so entangled in its own rich mythology; one failing of Apocalypse is that there are very few stories about Gaia or the Wyrm as anything other than forces and powers. With Forsaken, you know that you are the heirs of Father Wolf and his Firstborn, that you are daughters of mad Luna, that the Idigam you now face were banished by your father's will and the Hosts you fight were torn asunder in his jaws. The Pure don't fight you because they're evil or corrupted, but because they have a mythological need to destroy you (and they might be somewhat justified).<br /> <br /> Apocalypse wears a human facade. Forsaken spins a unique tale all its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T13:20:59-08:00","id":813599,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the appeal to Forsaken is that it distinctly lacks those elements you love so much. I suggest you stick with Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T13:38:30-08:00","id":813608,"title":"","content":"Well there's nothing wrong with sticking with Apocalypse:<br /> <br /> 1) Don't look to Forsaken to replace Apocalypse. It's not trying to. Its it's own game, with it's own concepts. There are lots of elements in Forsaken that can incorporate themes and elements you might enjoy, but they're never going to be Apocalypse. Part of that is what you might really get into with Forsaken isn't in the same place as it would have been in Apocalypse. For example Lodges (which are somewhat analogous to Apocalypse Camps) are where you get into cultural groups. So working in Lodges more strongly can help get some of those elements back in more than default.<br /> <br /> 2) Read Forsaken 2e. 1e was good, but 2e completely blew it out of the water. It really ramps up an evocative, and a inspiring setting. It's not Apocalypse. It's something different. It also hammers home that what Forsaken werewolves are, more than anything else: predators on the hunt. Getting away from the Apocalypse idea of packs was a huge help as well.<br /> <br /> 3) Remember that Forsaken is meant to be much more of a toolkit. What's lacking, and what's stressed, can be changed without messing up the game more easily than might be readily apparent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T14:47:53-08:00","id":813670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813608#post813608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Remember that Forsaken is meant to be much more of a toolkit. What's lacking, and what's stressed, can be changed without messing up the game more easily than might be readily apparent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is so true. As an example relevant to your interests, OP, here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/809400-umaraha-e-the-children-of-the-worm\">Umaraha'e: The Children of the Worm</a> - A Mystery Cult that worships a being they call the Worm (or is that &quot;Wyrm?&quot;), a vast cosmic force of entropy and consumption. Ties into Mage.<br /> <br /> Check out the Hosts, too. Great foes for werewolves. Here's one I made up, replete with fiction to help inspire you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/790655-zibhesi-the-red-plague-the-heart-drinkers-the-mosquito-hosts\">Zibhesi: The Mosquito Hosts</a><br /> <br /> You might notice a little bit of Apocalypse in there, which is great because WTA was my favorite Old World setting, and had perhaps my favorite playable race in any game ever, the Mokol\u00e9.<br /> <br /> I've even made plans to run Apocalypse using the Forsaken 2E engine (CofD engine in general). You might find it fairly easy to translate using the <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/100710/Werewolf-Translation-Guide?term=werewolf+translation+guide\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf Translation Guide</a>, for instance, bringing some of your favorite elements into Forsaken.<br /> <br /> But if you want to take Forsaken on its own merits, read through the 2E core. You'll see that in losing the big picture, the game is a tightly focused, highly thematic game of supernatural hunters. The Wolf Must Hunt. Read the <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/138981/The-Idigam-Chronicle-Anthology?term=Idigam+Chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Idigam Chronicle Anthology</a> for lots of inspiration. The <i>idigam </i>are big, powerful, alien spirits capable of warping the nature of the things around them. Defeating them often means bringing together many packs and other allies, pulling out all the stops\u2014great for when you want to jump from a more local story to a larger-scale one for a chronicle. Their history ties into <i>Uratha </i>mythology in some fascinating ways: they're ancient spirits once imprisoned on the moon by Father Wolf, the great wolf-god from whom werewolves are descended.<br /> <br /> Also note that you can easily inject cultural trappings in any of the tribes or even auspices, individual packs, whole protectorates, etc. In my own game, set in the Pacific Northwest, a lot of the Native American history, culture, and mythology inform the spirit world and the werewolves in that region.<br /> <br /> Forsaken puts you in the pads of the consummate hunters. Werewolves descend from godlike spirits of Wolf and Moon. They are half-flesh, half-spirit beings capable of walking between worlds. Their most ancient imperative: hunt the realms as <i>Urfarah </i>once did. Be faithful to the hunt. Seek balance, Harmony, in all things. Keep the prey in its proper place, and maintain the fragile balance between realms. They wield spirit-magic and lupine ferocity as they battle spirits, humans, monstrous Claimed, the Hosts, and each other. They wear human skins but they are not human, nor are they wolf. They've become something different, greater perhaps, occupying a unique space in their world. They grow, they live, they love, they fight, and they die. Unlike spirits or humans, their forms are protean, yet they are not amorphous <i>idigam</i>. Like wolves and humans, they <i>feel</i>, because theirs is a life lived without reservations. You are Wolf, and the wolf must hunt. Werewolves can't and don't sit back and let the world come to them. They lope into the night, howling as a pack, taking what they need by the throat. Blood runs hot. Flesh parts and shifts, bones crack, breath steams from flaring nostrils. It's a dangerous world in the shadows, full of monsters human and inhuman ... and as werewolves, you hunt them all.<br /> <br /> The Sacred Hunt calls, brother. Raise your howl along with ours!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T15:24:20-08:00","id":813690,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you really want a global conspiracy to fight against you've got the God-Machine and the Seers of the Throne and Hunter groups and a bunch of other stuff from other gamelines that will slot into Forsaken mechanically just fine. The CoD setting is completely modular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:00:18-08:00","id":813719,"title":"","content":"You also have the <i>Maeljin</i>, terrible lords of the Wounds, whose very name defies werewolf understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:03:48-08:00","id":813722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813670#post813670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might notice a little bit of Apocalypse in there, which is great because WTA was my favorite Old World setting, and had perhaps my favorite playable race in any game ever, the Mokol\u00e9.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which brings up another point; NWoD/CofD changing breeds kinda sucked. Any chance of a 2ed? I really WANT to like these games, because the mechanics are pretty good, but good crunch just doesn't help if I can't find interest in the fluff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:30:47-08:00","id":813747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813722#post813722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Which brings up another point; NWoD/CofD changing breeds kinda sucked. Any chance of a 2ed? I really WANT to like these games, because the mechanics are pretty good, but good crunch just doesn't help if I can't find interest in the fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting you say that, because Changing Breeds is generally considered to be poor because it was basically just Apocalypse in nWoD, and the two settings aren't designed to mesh. (Plus mechanical problems, but that's a side issue.) So I'm not sure which elements you are/aren't looking for in CofD Werewolf. <br /> <br /> Whether there'll be some 2E version of CB is unknown. There are many elements of the setting we need to give the 2E treatment to before we get to how to build/play a myriad of other shapeshifters. <br /> <br /> I say this as a fan of both lines - they're very different beasts with different themes, intentions and focuses. They're meant to be different, but 1E Forsaken had a lot of legacy elements from Apocalypse. We've refined and excised many of these, to better clarify what 2E is meant to be. <br /> <br /> I'd echo the sentiment above - get a copy of 2E and give it a read through. It's tighter, clearer, and better than 1E in every way (IMO). If it still doesn't grab you, for whatever reason (including not Apocalypse enough), then it might just not be the game for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:41:19-08:00","id":813753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813747#post813747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I say this as a fan of both lines - they're very different beasts with different themes, intentions and focuses. They're meant to be different, but 1E Forsaken had a lot of legacy elements from Apocalypse. We've refined and excised many of these, to better clarify what 2E is meant to be.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. I've never had much to do with Apocalypse and, in developing W:TF 2e there were a few bits of the game that I looked at and asked 'but what even is this about?' where the answer turned out to be just 'it was something held over from Apocalypse'. A lot of that stuff has now been sliced away.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T17:24:24-08:00","id":813768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813753#post813753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. I've never had much to do with Apocalypse and, in developing W:TF 2e there were a few bits of the game that I looked at and asked 'but what even is this about?' where the answer turned out to be just 'it was something held over from Apocalypse'. A lot of that stuff has now been sliced away.</div> </div> </div> </div>And quite honestly, for the better, in my opinion. (And I, too, say that as a fan of both lines.)<br /> <br /> To the OP: really, the best advice given in this thread (and has been echoed) is to grab a copy of 2e and see if it hooks you. Obviously, that's the idea, and that's what we were shooting for when we wrote it, but not all games are for all people in the end.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you then have specific questions about the material in the book, that's much easier for us to answer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T17:37:15-08:00","id":813771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813722#post813722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings up another point; NWoD/CofD changing breeds kinda sucked. Any chance of a 2ed? I really WANT to like these games, because the mechanics are pretty good, but good crunch just doesn't help if I can't find interest in the fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea if it'd sell well enough. It was bashed on mechanically and thematically, although I think there was a lot of good in there. If they ever did a 2E, I'd love to head it up, since I have lots of great ideas for Changing Breeds and it's one of my favorite topics. I wouldn't hold your breath, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T20:35:08-08:00","id":813878,"title":"","content":"So, I'm getting a lot of &quot;pick up W:tF 2ed&quot;, but I need to point out that until Onyx Path books are sold in stores again, that is NOT happening. I already bought 1ed and never use it, NO WAY am I buying a non-refundable PDF with no guarantee that I won't be wasting my money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T20:45:50-08:00","id":813883,"title":"","content":"Okay then, sorry we couldn't be of more help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T20:59:00-08:00","id":813887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813878#post813878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm getting a lot of &amp;quot;pick up W:tF 2ed&amp;quot;, but I need to point out that until Onyx Path books are sold in stores again, that is NOT happening. I already bought 1ed and never use it, NO WAY am I buying a non-refundable PDF with no guarantee that I won't be wasting my money.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally get your sentiment on this, but I am going to offer you three counterpoints. I'll preface that these are things to consider, and I won't be at all offended if you disagree, it's personal preference. I also say this as someone who never &quot;got&quot; Forsaken until 2e.<br /> <br /> 1) This is the easier of the two. Instead of buying Forsaken 2e, read the OpenDev articles first. This will give some of the flavour of the game and is what got me hooked on it in the first place. <br /> <br /> 2) Consider picking up the short story Anthology, which comes as a PDF at measly $3. <br /> <br /> 3) If you dig it after that, consider picking up the PDF, but don't look at it as a gaming investment (necessarily). Consider it a story, a world that you are reading about. The PDF is $20, and I'd say there is way more than that in world building, myth, and setting. I'd suggest that if you enjoy reading it then it's not wasted money. That is up to you to decide though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T21:44:21-08:00","id":813906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813690#post813690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if you really want a global conspiracy to fight against you've got the God-Machine and the Seers of the Throne and Hunter groups and a bunch of other stuff from other gamelines that will slot into Forsaken mechanically just fine. The CoD setting is completely modular.</div> </div> </div> </div>You always can use few connected Idigams to make secret conspiracy. Especially with Lodge of Quicksilver as cultists of Idigams - they believe that Child of Moon and Wolf was Idigam itself that somehow possesed human and passed it to it's ofspring. And now we have werewolf race... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T22:04:35-08:00","id":813913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813887#post813887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally get your sentiment on this, but I am going to offer you three counterpoints. I'll preface that these are things to consider, and I won't be at all offended if you disagree, it's personal preference. I also say this as someone who never &quot;got&quot; Forsaken until 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this - I was myself &quot;interested&quot; in some <b>Werewolf</b> game, tried 1ED for few sessions, but in the end <b>Mage</b> eat me. Now I run two <b>Mage</b> chronicles, instead of at least one of <b>Werewolf </b>2ED, only because I plan to make Modern-Vikings interconnected game about Malejin corruption inside Tribes of Moon and Pure - but to this <b>Dark Eras</b> book will be blessing. I even got whole <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths\">Norse Mythology based alternatives Uratha myths of Scandinavia region</a> ready. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm so much psyched for the Viking and Roman werewolves to come to our hands with <b>Dark Eras</b> book! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813887#post813887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) This is the easier of the two. Instead of buying Forsaken 2e, read the OpenDev articles first. This will give some of the flavour of the game and is what got me hooked on it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree - it's OpenDev that made me rethink if I really should look over <b>Forsaken</b> 2ED after my initial disapointment with 1ED corebook. And even when I count each and every zloty I have in mine pocket - I do not regrets spent on <b>Forsaken</b> 2ED. Even if you run Mage now, the rules for Spirits are valuable, the universe is great - and the coming of the &quot;lost and rampaging werewolves&quot; from the film really adds depth game which do not had <b>Apocalypse </b>before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813887#post813887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) If you dig it after that, consider picking up the PDF, but don't look at it as a gaming investment (necessarily). Consider it a story, a world that you are reading about. The PDF is $20, and I'd say there is way more than that in world building, myth, and setting. I'd suggest that if you enjoy reading it then it's not wasted money. That is up to you to decide though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine cWoD buddy says that <b>Forsaken</b> has superior mechanics and few setting elements that he likes very much. So he just want to mix and match both mythologies - just like users <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/743317-werewolf-the-apocasaken-mixing-mashing-and-seasoning-to-taste\">do on this forum</a> - I really look forward for this. I'm, myself, plan to upgrade <b>Apocalypse</b> Tribes as Forsaken Lodges, especially Scandinavian ones. There is so much you an make with this game system it blows my mind! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T22:31:53-08:00","id":813923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813722#post813722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really WANT to like these games, because the mechanics are pretty good, but good crunch just doesn't help if I can't find interest in the fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you taken a look at the 20th Anniversary edition of Werewolf the Apocalypse? It combines a modern rule set with the original setting that you like. It may be closer to what you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T22:45:54-08:00","id":813928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813887#post813887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Consider picking up the short story Anthology, which comes as a PDF at measly $3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd recommend this, too, but I'm a little biased. I'm quite happy with my story and definitely want to share that. Everyone's stories were very good and you wouldn't find a better snapshot of how cool Forsaken can be than the Anthology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T23:01:41-08:00","id":813932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813923#post813923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you taken a look at the 20th Anniversary edition of Werewolf the Apocalypse? It combines a modern rule set with the original setting that you like. It may be closer to what you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to be more than factual with this, but the X20 books are not a modern rule-set. They're (so far at least) minor updates of the same rule-set from the 90s. W20 has some major improvements in it, but it isn't a new edition that tries to apply lessons learned in 20 years of design to the old games; it's an omnibus that collects Apocalypse core material in one tome with some tweaks here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T00:21:23-08:00","id":813956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813878#post813878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm getting a lot of &quot;pick up W:tF 2ed&quot;, but I need to point out that until Onyx Path books are sold in stores again, that is NOT happening. I already bought 1ed and never use it, NO WAY am I buying a non-refundable PDF with no guarantee that I won't be wasting my money.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, to be to fair you went into a forum where everyone is a WtF fan. Of course we would recommend the product to you especially since the majority of us love the change.<br /> <br /> Now, I understand that whether or not you get use out of the book is a big issue, because ultimately, no one wants to waste money. However, consider this. Even if you don't like the setting of the book, you can jury rig the entire game to play Apocalypse with some relatively easy conversion. The thing comes with its own internal core rule book so you don't need to waste cash getting the new Chronicles of Darkness book if you don't want to invest in it too much. So purchasing the book for the <i>mechanics</i> is a valid choice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, the merits of the Forsaken core are that ultimately, I'd argue that it let's you be a werewolf better than Apocalypse does. Now, I know that may bother you an Apocalypse fan, but hear me out.<br /> <br /> By your own words, Apocalypse puts you in the role of a Defender of Gaia, one of a chosen many that exists to protect the world. You're given a cosmic charge and you fight against forces of corruption of your world in an effort to try to fix it. The scope is global and you work towards the goal of defeating a cosmological force with your brethren all over the world. Forgive me if I may, but consider... how many other fictional or folklore works other than Apocalypse do that?<br /> <br /> <br /> In constrast, Forsaken is a little more humble. You are a hunter, because you inherited a fraction of an ancient hunter spirit's power. You are driven to pursue your goals and what you hunt is ultimately up to you; whether it be for flesh, power... enjoyment against foes both in the real and spiritual realms. You fight against others of your own kind for territory because territory is a resource, a sign of prestige, and ultimately a tool to help you select targets. You are not a border patrol guard against spirits, no, you chase spirits that get into your territory because ultimately, it's <i>yours</i> and if they're going to be there, they have to follow your rules or scat.<br /> <br /> Aside from the spiritual backdrop, the idea of Werewolf the Forsaken 2e is much more commonly found in werewolf media and symbolism: the idea of the wolf as the hunter and the master of its territory. When you play the game, this is the role you play, a wolf.<br /> <br /> I will be the first to admit I might have been overly harsh and judgemental against Apocalypse in the above. It has its merits and it appeals to a different style of play than Forsaken does, but as I said, I do not think Apocalypse portrays you playing a werewolf as cleanly as Forsaken does. You have animalism in both games, that's true, but that's something nearly all of the World of Darkness games can get, the ability to turn into an animal.<br /> <br /> My statement is thus, does Forsaken cling closer and play true to the ideal of being a werewolf more than Apocalpyse does? And if Forsaken is closer to the ideal, would you, as a self proclaimed fan of werecreatures, consider that a valid reason to purchase the book despite lacking a few of the trappings of Apocalpyse, namely the global scope, the cosmic forces, and the lack of metaplot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 01-22-2016, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T02:25:17-08:00","id":814002,"title":"","content":"There is one suggestion I have that I don't think I've seen from anyone else yet.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know any good W:tF Actual Plays Mangle77 could read? Actual Plays that exemplify the strengths of Werewolf: the Forsaken?<br /> <br /> I admit that myself, I don't always 'grok' a gameline right away, but in my experience a really good Actual Play can really bring a gameline alive for me, showing off what can be done with the material. (This may also be why the settings chapters in the 2nd editions tend to be my favorites, showing off examples of how to put all the pieces together.)<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, while I do have a Werewolf: the Forsaken AP on my to-read list, I haven't actually read it yet, so I'm reluctant to recommend it. That said, this is the W:tF forum. Surely someone here knows of a W:tF Actual Play they love or feel exemplifies W:tF's strengths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T04:47:16-08:00","id":814044,"title":"","content":"I'm not aware of any APs for 2nd edition, though I know of several for 1st. <br /> <br /> It's a good suggestion, but I doubt any 1E APs are going to greatly inform Mangle77, as he already has 1E. <br /> <br /> If anyone has 2E APs, I'd love to know for my own interest as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T06:18:52-08:00","id":814080,"title":"","content":"There's a few podcasts of my Paris Forsaken game but it only goes to the 9th session because the chap whose website it is that hosts the podcast ran out of space to host more for the time being.<br /> <br /> Note that since i\u200bt's a podcast it doesn't benefit from the bit in a written AP where you get everything nicely summarised down etc; podcasts have the whole shebang of all the random whargarbl, the dice rolls, the bits where the ST forgets a rule for a bit or has an argument with a player, etc etc :P Also we have a toddler who sometimes likes to, er, be involved.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh yeah, so the url\u200b for anyone brave enough to listen is \u200b<span style=\"font-size:10px\">https://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com/</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T09:22:49-08:00","id":814177,"title":"","content":"I've recently discovered the In Sanity We Trust podcasts while looking for various CoD AP it's so useful to see a game in action and has helped me grasp the concepts for the games that originally i may not have got just from a reading. I've not got any experience of WtA so I've no real frame of reference but by the time I'd finished listening to the Paris Chronicle it was enough to have me sold on Werewolf the Forsaken 2ed in fact I think it will likely be my first CoD game I attempt to run so I definitely recommend giving them a listen. (If you enjoy them I'd also suggest you give there Mummy AP a listen because Mahu is amazing.)<br /> <br /> Is there anyway we can donate towards web-hosting for the site? I'd love to hear more from you and your group I was gutted when I ran out of podcasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7354-monsieurcutts","name":"MonsieurCutts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7354_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:02:14-08:00","id":814210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonsieurCutts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814177#post814177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently discovered the In Sanity We Trust podcasts while looking for various CoD AP it's so useful to see a game in action and has helped me grasp the concepts for the games that originally i may not have got just from a reading. I've not got any experience of WtA so I've no real frame of reference but by the time I'd finished listening to the Paris Chronicle it was enough to have me sold on Werewolf the Forsaken 2ed in fact I think it will likely be my first CoD game I attempt to run so I definitely recommend giving them a listen. (If you enjoy them I'd also suggest you give there Mummy AP a listen because Mahu is amazing.)<br /> <br /> Is there anyway we can donate towards web-hosting for the site? I'd love to hear more from you and your group I was gutted when I ran out of podcasts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Uh, good question. I'll have to ask.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:21:58-08:00","id":814228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813599#post813599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the appeal to Forsaken is that it distinctly lacks those elements you love so much. I suggest you stick with Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">It's a &quot;sell me&quot; thread, not a &quot;dissuade me&quot; thread Ephsy. Don't thread crap.\u200b</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:29:46-08:00","id":814236,"title":"","content":"I would have written an argument, but OP distinctly picked every element of the game that differs Forsaken from Apocalypse, almost deliberately, it seems. So I don't get the need to try to sell it when, by OP's own admission, won't give the game a try. Nothing wrong with knowing what you like and sticking with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:39:31-08:00","id":814316,"title":"","content":"I've thought long and hard about how to explain what I like about Forsaken when we both come from such different places with what we enjoy or don't enjoy in these two games. I think I've finally come up with something though. You've mentioned you're a fan of the original changing breeds from Apocalypse. What I loved about Changing Breeds has been turned into the entire theme of Forsaken.<br /> <br /> In Apocalypse, back in the beginning the Garou lost control of their inner nature and began the War of Rage against the other Changing Breeds. Because of this mistake they turned their allies against them and broke apart the alliance the Gaia herself had created. It was a terrible horrible mistake that may have doomed the entire world. Except the Garou didn't give up and wring their hands in despair. They did their very best to fix the problem they had created. They took on the duties of the kindred that they slayed, they tried to do things that they'd never been meant to do and they kept at it for millenia. To a lesser extent you can see the same thing in the Imperium, where werewolves hunted mankind to keep the population low but only succeeded in turning mankind against Gaia as well.<br /> <br /> I think that this was a really valuable lesson to include in Apocalypse and it really fit with the environmental themes of that book. After all, we as humans have made terrible mistakes in preserving the environment. We've wiped out species and disrupted the ecological balance of the world. It was a good lesson in how to not dwell on our failure but instead to look around us and start solving the problems that we can solve.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, this drama took center stage in the death of Father Wolf. The Forsaken were given an impossible choice. The human side of them told them to love their father, the wolf side of them told them to challenge a weak leader. This internal conflict is the new theme of Werewolf for the WtF editions. Now instead of struggling against the external foe of the Wyrm, the true challenge for any Werewolf is now an internal struggle about being divided between Human and Wolf, Flesh and Spirit. Much like the Garou (and unlike the Pure), the Forsaken didn't give up when faced with this impossible challenge. They challenged Father Wolf, as they had to do, but the important part is that they also understood that they would have to pay the price and seek atonement for this action.<br /> <br /> Everything the Forsaken are doing today is continuing this ancient atonement, seeking forgiveness not by endlessly apologizing or dwelling on the past but instead by moving forwards and doing what they can to fix it. Likewise their true enemy isn't spirits, ghosts, shards, the claimed or even the Idigam. The true enemy is their own divided nature and the eternal challenge of seeking Harmony.<br /> <br /> I think the most important thing about Werewolf never changed and that's the lesson that you never give up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813932#post813932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to be more than factual with this, but the X20 books are not a modern rule-set. They're (so far at least) minor updates of the same rule-set from the 90s. W20 has some major improvements in it, but it isn't a new edition that tries to apply lessons learned in 20 years of design to the old games; it's an omnibus that collects Apocalypse core material in one tome with some tweaks here and there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that I disagree with you on the facts at all, I just interpret them a little differently. I agree that they were very conservative about changing the rules because they were attempting to preserve something that people loved rather than recreating it anew. They definitely adopted a policy of &quot;if it ain't broke don't fix it&quot; but I still think you can see the twenty years of experience used in recognizing the places where it was broken and finding the best possible way to fix the problems while changing as little as possible.<br /> <br /> While it's not what I'm looking for personally (thus why I play Chronicles of Darkness now), for someone like our OP who is very much in love with the original line but wants some cleaned up systems it could potentially be perfect. Anyway, I thought it worth mentioning just on the off chance that our OP had never heard of them. I know when they first came out I thought there was no point in buying them because I still have my original World of Darkness books. It wasn't until a friend of mine showed me V20 that I realized that they'd made some fixes and streamlined the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:49:18-08:00","id":814326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813878#post813878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm getting a lot of &quot;pick up W:tF 2ed&quot;, but I need to point out that until Onyx Path books are sold in stores again, that is NOT happening. I already bought 1ed and never use it, NO WAY am I buying a non-refundable PDF with no guarantee that I won't be wasting my money.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one seems to have mentioned the Idigam, the big, bad, world fucking engines of destruction that are the main large scale antagonists of the book. There's plenty of backstory available in the corebook, along with multiple setting locale information for those that want to play in an area of the world that are different from home. The difference between them and the Wyrm is that you don't require the entire Garou Nation to go down in order to achieve a victory against them, but you do need some outside co-operation to get it done. I like games that give the PC's a realistic chance of still being alive at the end of the story, something that wasn't really possible if you went directly against the Wyrm. If you let metaplot get in the way the PC's were observers in the grand scheme of things, real change was always brought about by signature characters. Forsaken lets the PC's take center stage in a way that Apocalypse rarely did, and Apocalypse was my main gameline in CWoD. I liked following the metaplot, but playing it wasn't as entertaining as reading it. Forsaken gets away form that and that's a selling point to me.<br /> <br /> Now, if you like the Cosmic level antagonists they are still available, but the burden of setting up the conflict resides with the ST. It's their job to make sure there is a point to the story, not some random supplement that may suddenly change the direction you were taking the chronicle because new info invalidates events in your story (if you are trying to use the 'canon' setting material). The Maeljin are still present, but are left up to the ST to define at the moment beyond some very brief write-ups in 1e (Blasphemies and Lore of the Forsaken) and Inferno. They aren't statted up so that players can just kill to add another notch to their &quot;how many gods I killed&quot; belt. If your ST wants to stat them up so their players can do that there is nothing stopping them from doing so, and if they do they aren't &quot;playing the game wrong&quot;. You can have your cake and eat it too, but you have to bake the cake yourself. Feel free to steal that as a sig.<br /> <br /> I'm also a fan of the shift of focus from being spirit cops to alpha predators/hunters, Gifts power scaling based on Renown so that Renown isn't an XP sink, Gift lists being thematically tied together, non werewolves now being able to participate in the pack, and the overall toughness buff that werewolves received compared to 1e. At the moment there is literally only one thing I would change from the core rules and it's a minor point (I have Gauru form claws count as magic based weaponry for certain game effects, like Vampires' damage downgrading, but not the other forms' claws. Personal preference that doesn't impact the game all that much.)<br /> <br /> As for future supplements I'd like to see, a Predators like book that covers the Pure in more depth along with all of the Firstborn totems and other spirit pro/antagonists, another that covers Bale Hounds and the Maeljin (to add the Apocalypse like flavor back, some people did like those elements, just not in the core rules), and then something to go over the way Lodges work in the current rules setup (I kind of expect The Pack to have a bit of what I'm looking for, Chris, Claire and Bunyip may have info they can share on that at some future date). A big Hunting Grounds book that covers differences in the way Tribes go about their hunts in urban vs rural environments would be nice too.<br /> <br /> <br /> edit, I missed Wyrdhamster's mention of the Idigam. My bad. And Claire's too. Goddammit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 01-22-2016, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:36:24-08:00","id":814387,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be honest, the &quot;Uratha are just spirit border patrol cops&quot; thing has about as much validity to it as &quot;Gauru are just furry planeteers&quot;. When you boil the central conflict of a setting down to a simple glib analogy, of course it's going to make the setting sound lame.<br /> <br /> What Forsaken 2e did to win me over that neither 1e or Apocalypse was able to do to my satisfaction was let me play a horror movie werewolf. Then, it took it a step further and gave me a versimilar reason for my horror movie werewolf to transition into a proud member of the complex werewolf culture that the game set up. I can start out a clueless bloke who just went through his first change and is terrified of what he's become, tries to fight his nature, and then gets introduced to the ways of The People, who teach him to balance his human side with his spirit/wolf side. He can slowly learn why it's important to maintain the barrier between the worlds of spirit and flesh within his territory, he can join a Tribe that knows why a particular kind of prey is most dangerous and how best to hunt them. He can take time to learn about his newfound cultural heritage, and <i>it will all make sense from a character development perspective.</i> <br /> <br /> That's what I love about Forsaken, and about 2e in particular. It completely skirts the comparisons to Captain Planet and Yu Yu Hakusho by presenting a clear and intuitive-feeling path from ordinary human to Luna's chosen predator (or Gaia's chosen warrior, if you like). Instead of that abrupt, jarring &quot;You didn't think it would be like in the movies, did you?&quot; Moment, it eases you into learning what it means to be a werewolf in this setting. And that is fucking awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-22-2016, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T13:01:34-08:00","id":814410,"title":"","content":"&quot;Movie werewolves&quot; was also a thing that sold me to <b>Forsaken</b> 2ED. I <i>love</i> Wolf Blooded as typical ( lot less powerful ) &quot;cursed&quot; werewolves of movies. I <i>love</i> I can make ordinary human &quot;sick&quot; with &quot;werewolf curse&quot; in-game setting and it will make sense without hereditary needed in 1ED or <b>Apocalypse</b> ( well, it is <i>there</i>, but lot less hidden <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I <i>love</i> extreme imbalanced Uratha ideas being &quot;this cursed guy that kills whole village and do not remember this after that&quot; or &quot;the terrifying shape shifting spiritual monster&quot; on both endings of Harmony. And I love that I finally play a real urban predator that <b><i>hunts</i></b>, and not just slash hies enemies with claws. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Also, I love that even inhuman Predator Kings wolves of Pure now will have human Touchstones. I really need to put this Predator Kings NPC &quot;ultimate hunter&quot; idea I have - and then show the players that at the end of the night he returns to the trailer where his fist school daughter sleeps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Being more wolf-like made werewolf extremely more human, in <b>Forsaken</b> 2ED. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T13:16:47-08:00","id":814417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814326#post814326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one seems to have mentioned the Idigam, the big, bad, world fucking engines of destruction that are the main large scale antagonists of the book.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> edit, I missed Wyrdhamster's mention of the Idigam. My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield, from post #6</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you want to take Forsaken on its own merits, read through the 2E core. You'll see that in losing the big picture, the game is a tightly focused, highly thematic game of supernatural hunters. The Wolf Must Hunt. Read the <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/138981/The-Idigam-Chronicle-Anthology?term=Idigam+Chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Idigam Chronicle Anthology</a> for lots of inspiration. The <i>idigam </i>are big, powerful, alien spirits capable of warping the nature of the things around them. Defeating them often means bringing together many packs and other allies, pulling out all the stops\u2014great for when you want to jump from a more local story to a larger-scale one for a chronicle. Their history ties into <i>Uratha </i>mythology in some fascinating ways: they're ancient spirits once imprisoned on the moon by Father Wolf, the great wolf-god from whom werewolves are descended.</div> </div> </div> </div>:P<br /> <br /> Although my description of them as &quot;spirits,&quot; even alien ones, is just a useful shorthand. The <i>idigam </i>defy any simple explanation by their very nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T15:20:02-08:00","id":814483,"title":"","content":"Sorry Claire, I literally skipped over that entire paragraph when reading your post. In my defense I had just woken up and misread a few posts, at least you got a namedrop in my orginal post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T16:32:16-08:00","id":814528,"title":"","content":"Even if you don't want to use the idigam, though I enjoy them a lot, you still have spirits. And once you get to rank 5 you're basically dealing with gods, with still a few ranks left to play. If you want to bring across a Wyrm analogue it wouldn't be that difficult. Just have one of the gods act.<br /> <br /> But everything's really been said.<br /> <br /> Big draw for me is that the book really gets the 'feel' of playing a predator across. But I was already way sold on Werewolf the Forsaken since first edition, with my long interest in animism and its clear influence on the spirit and Shadow. I never cared for Apocalypse beyond an interest in Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T18:02:43-08:00","id":814564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814483#post814483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry Claire, I literally skipped over that entire paragraph when reading your post. In my defense I had just woken up and misread a few posts, at least you got a namedrop in my orginal post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5tSa3xLVYgM\" data-code=\"5tSa3xLVYgM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5tSa3xLVYgM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I do intend to write up stuff bringing Pentex and other bits across, and I think I have an idea for the Wyld analogue, if the Abyss is the Wyrm and the God-Machine is sort of like the Weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 01-22-2016, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T19:08:20-08:00","id":814593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814564#post814564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do intend to writeup stuff bringing Pentex and other bits across</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh cool. Pentex was always one of my favourite bits in W:tA. I'd enjoy seeing them in Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T20:21:37-08:00","id":814625,"title":"","content":"I mean, one of the greater issues that OP is going to run into is the fact that he's unwilling to buy any books that he can't return, which means anything from OPP is right out, whether it's Forsaken 2e, W20, or what have you. There's stuff to look at, like the open development journals for werewolf specific stuff and the free god-machine update PDF to check out the base CofD system, but if the PDF/PoD model isn't going to work for him then there's really not much we can do.<br /> <br /> I want to reiterate something that people have said before, because it can't be restated enough: Forsaken is -not- Apocalypse, and wasn't meant to replace Apocalypse. You can be forgiven for thinking that if you saw how the Requiem core handled Vampire, and Forsaken got stuck with a -lot- of stuff that it didn't really need because the early writers didn't know how far they could stretch, but even at that point they were trying very hard to make Forsaken it's own game, and by Awakening and on each nWoD game stood as it's own thing. So I would recommend, as others have, that if you check it out that you look at it as a game to be judged on it's own merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 01-22-2016, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T22:29:20-08:00","id":814669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814564#post814564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5tSa3xLVYgM\" data-code=\"5tSa3xLVYgM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5tSa3xLVYgM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I do intend to write up stuff bringing Pentex and other bits across, and I think I have an idea for the Wyld analogue, if the Abyss is the Wyrm and the God-Machine is sort of like the Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200b <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ed5Bh_DbHPU\" data-code=\"Ed5Bh_DbHPU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ed5Bh_DbHPU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T00:42:43-08:00","id":814703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814625#post814625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, one of the greater issues that OP is going to run into is the fact that he's unwilling to buy any books that he can't return, which means anything from OPP is right out, whether it's Forsaken 2e, W20, or what have you. There's stuff to look at, like the open development journals for werewolf specific stuff and the free god-machine update PDF to check out the base CofD system, but if the PDF/PoD model isn't going to work for him then there's really not much we can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/chroniclesofdarkness/werewolftheforsaken/page/4/\" target=\"_blank\">Open Development articles</a> are answer here - each one of the highlight major changes between 1ED and 2ED. They also - mostly - are what 2ED ended with on ideas. And highlight the strong places of <b>Forsaken</b> as the system.<br /> <br /> In mine own example, the <b>Changeling: The Lost</b> 2ED highlighted me changes to the system I may like ( detaching Kiths from Seemings ) but also those that I may not like ( some implications the Seemings have on personality and need for &quot;Escape Narrative&quot; ). In the end, I probably will try <b>Lost</b> 2ED, but I'm more informed consumer and I know in what I'm packing before reading the corebook - instead of whining &quot;oh, they took out mine favorite Contract&quot;. <b>Chronicles of Darkness </b>games are each one of them their own beasts ( pun intended <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and some little groundwork in reviewing them makes you much more appreciate.<br /> <br /> Also, it cool to read what Devs have in their mind when writing the game. And if Open Dev is at present - like in <b>Hunter the Vigil</b> 2ED - it's great to have a voice in shaping the next Edition of the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T00:43:11-08:00","id":814704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814625#post814625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to reiterate something that people have said before, because it can't be restated enough: Forsaken is -not- Apocalypse, and wasn't meant to replace Apocalypse. You can be forgiven for thinking that if you saw how the Requiem core handled Vampire, and Forsaken got stuck with a -lot- of stuff that it didn't really need because the early writers didn't know how far they could stretch, but even at that point they were trying very hard to make Forsaken it's own game, and by Awakening and on each nWoD game stood as it's own thing. So I would recommend, as others have, that if you check it out that you look at it as a game to be judged on it's own merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI disagree to a small degree here, because when NWoD was launched it was specifically stated that the devs were designing the games how they would have developed the original lines if they had the knowledge they accumulated over 10+ years of development, the new lines were meant as replacements for the old lines. Requiem certainly was a replacement, and let's not overlook the Tremere being put back in with the Mages rather than Vampires, somewhere they would play better.<br /> Consider how much of Apocalypse's flavor was brought back through supplements like War Against the Pure and The Pure, and the inclusion of the Maeljin. The Pure in particular have elements that worked with the BSD's while removing a lot of the ick factor (but not all IMO, they were still antagonist splats). The Bale Hounds were where they dumped the real ick factor stuff. The Pure also took the less savory aspects of the Garou Tribes, Ivory Claws seem like SIlver Fangs and Shadow lords combined into one, Predator Kings are Get of Fenris and Wendigo influenced, Fire Touched have more than a bit of Bone Gnawer DNA, and the Pure as a whole feel like they were influenced by the Red Talons. The devs wanted to ditch what they felt didn't work and tweak what did. The second editions were where they really differentiated the product lines and are making them clearly their own entities, it's why I think the OP should at least check out Forsaken 2e as it's quite a different beast than 1e. To me it feels like an evolutionary step rather than an iterative one.<br /> <br /> And the joking aside, I'\u200bm interested in seeing what Claire writes up, I see Promethean's The Principle as being roughly analogous to the Wyld in CoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 01-23-2016, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T01:21:33-08:00","id":814712,"title":"","content":"Mm. Well, that's quite possible. I've always heard it the way I described but I admit I came onboard somewhere in the Changeling/Hunter days, and by that point the games were designed to stand on their own merits. The way I've always perceived it after the fact was that Forsaken got the shaft out of the original three - Requiem made it's changes with a scalpel to create a very similar experience to Masquerade with a slightly different focus, while Mage was a whole different game*. Forsaken feels like it's torn between trying to redo Apocalypse and being a new thing, and suffered immensely for it.<br /> <br /> I think Ethan Skemp said at one point that if he developed Werewolf in 2005 like he had developed Changeling in 2007 Forsaken would have been an entirely different beast, but I can't find the quote now.<br /> <br /> * Again, you could be forgiven for thinking otherwise due to Awakening 1e having possibly the worst core book WW has -ever- put out, and also in no small part because it reused a LOT of terminology (despite the concepts being significantly different from their previous counterparts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 01-23-2016, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T02:05:18-08:00","id":814729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=813753#post813753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. I've never had much to do with Apocalypse and, in developing W:TF 2e there were a few bits of the game that I looked at and asked 'but what even is this about?' where the answer turned out to be just 'it was something held over from Apocalypse'. A lot of that stuff has now been sliced away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep hearing this. I never liked 1e <b>Werewolf</b> and I never took a look at <b>Werewolf the Apocalypse</b> until the W20 books were out and then being sold on 2e <b>Werewolf</b>.<br /> <br /> So simply out of the sake of curiosity, what were some holdovers from the 'previous' game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T04:14:42-08:00","id":814766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814564#post814564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)the God-Machine is sort of like the Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, the more time passes, the more I think about making a write-up connecting Creator Wolf from sourcebook with God-Machine.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814729#post814729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So simply out of the sake of curiosity, what were some holdovers from the 'previous' game?</div> </div> </div> </div>W:tF 1ed felt directionless. Differences are really just a number of small things that overall add a lot to how the game is approached and played. In W:tA tribes were defined by their ideology and cultural aspects: Uktena were indians, Black Furies were feminists, Children of Gaia were human-clinging Greenpeace activists, Bone Gnawers were hobbos living on the street (I'm purposefully simplifying, please don't explode over those parallels). It carried in some way to the W:tF, differences were significant between editions, but a lot felt that new tribes are just a mix of portions of old tribes and given a motto by which they lived, while being mostly stripped from the ideological/cultural background of the predecessors. That's why Iron Masters could be percieved by some as mix of Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers or Blood Talons as mix of Fianna, Get of Fenris and Red Talons.<br /> <br /> Tribes were there on the stage of character creation, but their overall impact on the game itself wasn't big, since it was all about the pack now and not about the tribes anymore. But they were in a new game, put in a bit of a limbo of being significant and at the same time not at all.<br /> <br /> In 2ed tribes from 1ed were defined by what they hunt. It was one of those &quot;small, but big&quot; changes since suddenly when you were playing Hunter in the Darkness you weren't <i> &quot;a stealhy hunter guy who protects the wilds and who never belonged before first change, but also sometimes inhabits city and protects significant things there and also...&quot;</i>, but &quot;you are psycho killer from slasher films killing swarms of rat/spider demons&quot;. Now when in your chronicle pack of Hunters in the Darkness will appear in a territory, your players will immediately think &quot;OH MY GOLLY, @%#^ IS GOING DOWN&quot; because everybody knows why they are here and what they go for.<br /> <br /> In W:tA there were alphas as leaders of the pack, W:tF 1ed mentions those in few places (actually even at the beginning, in the tribes description) and even though from the read you are supposed to think that packs function a bit differently and alpha concept isn't as significant in W:tF, a concept still is present there and packs are made of werewolves only with some sort of leader on the hunt. Different than W:tA, but there are similarities. So while W:tF wolf-blooded aren't kinfolk, they fundamentally still function as breeding machines for furry superhumans.<br /> <br /> 2ed puts alpha term to trash and packs can consist of werewolves, wolf-blooded and even (non)ordinary humans and now everybody adds to the hunt. PCs with different tribes add to it different and wolf-blooded have some powers that werewolves never will have. Every wolf-blooded now has some distinct, werewolfy feature (Tell) that defines it. Moreover, people can become wolf-blooded due to the exposure to werewolves now, it's not only about blood lineage as previously.<br /> This is a game changer, since wolf-blooded can have very big impact on the chronicle and not be only &quot;ultimately a bit better than normal human helpers&quot;. Every wolf-blooded power is designed in a way to be potential plothook. Werewolves of which pack are murdering people on PCs territory? (None, it's a guy who became wolf-blooded after last PC action and who can now take one of the werewolf forms). There's a guy who is Pure slave that can sense hosts, every single one of them from 10 miles radius (Host-Ache tell). Forsaken must steal him to find out if they really destroyed Shartha during their last adventure.<br /> Oh and wolf-blooded and humans can perform or be part of some werewolf rituals. Suddenly capable and well organised wolf/moon cults are a thing in 2ed. <br /> <br /> Gifts. In W:tA and W:tF they worked on a scale from 1 to 5. In W:tF 2ed there's only linear progression in Moon Gifts and you get them for free, so you don't have curse of &quot;I will never get 5th!&quot;. Other Gifts (Shadow and Wolf) have Facets and they are unlocked if you have appropriate renown. They are also designed in specific way, more here:<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-...-the-forsaken/</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-...-the-forsaken/</a><br /> <br /> It's a big difference now between 1ed and 2ed, gifts are less of superpowers and more like aspects of wolf/werewolf that are in tales and trust me, they are very, very well designed. Hell, there's even a power that allows you to blow houses like a wolf from &quot;Three little pigs&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Nature worth saving&quot; trope from W:tA was a bit present in W:tF 1ed, especially as I said before around Hunters in the Darkness. Now there's 0 of that. Nature works as an ally of wolf/werewolf, but is a fucking scary place and a tool of hunt. Also a place that will terrify PCs themselves (Touchstone: Call of the Wild)<br /> <br /> Harmony is another aspect in which W:tF had some influence from W:tA even though W:tA didn't have morality mechanics. Oath of the Moon was a big deal in W:tA and remained in W:tF 1ed. In 2ed it seems to be less important for morality mechanics which by the way was redesigned completely and &quot;you should not eat human flesh&quot; is more of a social and narrative problem and mechanics itself show now cannibalism as a dillemma that is there and can be counted into PCs actions. In W:tA and W:tF it really wasn't a problem, no sane player would even think about it or eat anybody bar the really extreme situations.<br /> <br /> Erm...those were only on top of my head and already post seems to be too long.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: There's a lot of minor things in 1ed that were a tip towards W:tA, but that overall were unnecessary in W:tF. 2ed got rid of it altogether and gave game clear direction and distinct mood and atmosphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7871,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","user":"Miriander","date":".  proofreading 01-23-2016, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T06:37:43-08:00","id":814810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814712#post814712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Again, you could be forgiven for thinking otherwise due to Awakening 1e having possibly the worst core book WW has -ever- put out, and also in no small part because it reused a LOT of terminology (despite the concepts being significantly different from their previous counterparts).</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening 1e wasn't that bad. IMO it was better than Forsaken 1e. They were both better than Geist 1.0. The quality on that was so low a 1.5 came out almost immediately.<br /> <br /> More on topic. I've said it elsewhere but Forsaken 2.0 is the best RPG I've ever read and I've been playing, reading and collecting rpgs for 24 years. It literally has something that will interest every kind of player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T06:45:04-08:00","id":814814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814729#post814729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep hearing this. I never liked 1e <b>Werewolf</b> and I never took a look at <b>Werewolf the Apocalypse</b> until the W20 books were out and then being sold on 2e <b>Werewolf</b>.<br /> <br /> So simply out of the sake of curiosity, what were some holdovers from the 'previous' game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, one of the last examples I came across, a really small and simple one - the term 'klaive'.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T07:03:20-08:00","id":814817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814814#post814814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, one of the last examples I came across, a really small and simple one - the term 'klaive'.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, I am ridiculously glad we got rid of that term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T07:03:47-08:00","id":814819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814814#post814814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, one of the last examples I came across, a really small and simple one - the term 'klaive'.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hm, has it been replaced with a more appropriate term? One that's more grammatically correct with the rest of First Tongue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T07:26:36-08:00","id":814828,"title":"","content":"It's just a Fetish now, I think. If it had power, anyway. Otherwise it's just a sword. No need for a special word.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know if rolling for shapeshifting is one of those Apocalypse holdovers, but I'm glad it's gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 01-23-2016, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T08:07:44-08:00","id":814852,"title":"","content":"What's First Tongue for &quot;sword&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T08:35:22-08:00","id":814861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814852#post814852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's First Tongue for &quot;sword&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Sikla Akis' dictionary: Uhur","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T09:06:53-08:00","id":814866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814819#post814819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, has it been replaced with a more appropriate term? One that's more grammatically correct with the rest of First Tongue?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the line between &quot;fetish weapon&quot; and &quot;Klaive&quot; was never very clear in 1e. It was this weird term that would get applied to some special fetish weapons because reasons, and then it didn't actually do anything different than a normal fetish weapon. So, in 2e, they're all just fetish weapons. No need for a few of them to arbitrarily have a different name that doesn't mean anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-23-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T10:24:44-08:00","id":814902,"title":"","content":"It makes sense for 'warriors of Gaia' to have a separate name, considering the emphasis a warrior puts on a weapon. In Forsaken they are extensions of the Uratha's Shadow dealings, and whether they're an ax or a car or a paper airplane, they're used for the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T11:10:57-08:00","id":814945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814866#post814866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, the line between &quot;fetish weapon&quot; and &quot;Klaive&quot; was never very clear in 1e. It was this weird term that would get applied to some special fetish weapons because reasons, and then it didn't actually do anything different than a normal fetish weapon. So, in 2e, they're all just fetish weapons. No need for a few of them to arbitrarily have a different name that doesn't mean anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant to say, a &quot;proper&quot; First Tongue name. Granted, I guess maybe just &quot;Weapon&quot; is enough in the context of a werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T13:28:57-08:00","id":815000,"title":"","content":"I always saw a klaive as being not just a weapon, but a weapon whose specific primary purpose was killing other werewolves. That's how it was defined in my 1e game though it isn't particularly supported by any of the written material. It was a weapon of war, not just utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 01-23-2016, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T13:44:52-08:00","id":815009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814866#post814866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the line between &quot;fetish weapon&quot; and &quot;Klaive&quot; was never very clear in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was probably me just getting confused by old Apocalypse terminology, but I always assumed the difference was that it was a fetish weapon made out of silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:40:07-08:00","id":815043,"title":"","content":"And that confusion and lack of proper definition, or division from other fetish weapons, is exactly why we got rid of the term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:47:53-08:00","id":815050,"title":"","content":"But should not general &quot;Fetish Weapons&quot; have First Tongue term?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:51:28-08:00","id":815054,"title":"","content":"The term used to be klaive, in 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815043#post815043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that confusion and lack of proper definition, or division from other fetish weapons, is exactly why we got rid of the term.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never met anyone confused by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:13:46-08:00","id":815066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815054#post815054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term used to be klaive, in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were Fetish weapons that were not Klaives, so evidently it was not the general term for fetish weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815054#post815054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never met anyone confused by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen a few in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T16:47:47-08:00","id":815111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815054#post815054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term used to be klaive, in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're replying to wyrdhamster's post immediately above yours, 'klaive' was never the First Tongue term for anything. It was a nonsense word when viewed through the lens of how Forsaken named other things. (There are exceptions that still exist - these are mostly Apocalypse holdovers, but they tended to have meaning that still mattered to the game.)<br /> <br /> Part of the problem was that every klaive was a fetish weapon, but not every fetish weapon was a klaive. Plus there was no definition of what a klaive was in Forsaken, or why it would be distinct from any other fetish weapon. Finally, klaives had no real purpose in Forsaken. In Apocalypse, Gaia's warriors clashing with oversized silver swords was thematic-heavy-metal-over-the-top awesomeness. In Forsaken it was a weird anachronism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T18:29:26-08:00","id":815165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815111#post815111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're replying to wyrdhamster's post immediately above yours, 'klaive' was never the First Tongue term for anything. It was a nonsense word when viewed through the lens of how Forsaken named other things. (There are exceptions that still exist - these are mostly Apocalypse holdovers, but they tended to have meaning that still mattered to the game.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is kinda too bad that the name of the Killing Form is one such term. Fortunately, it *could* be First Tongue for Gift of the Wolf's Mouth, which is a pretty cool name for the form. Still, I would have liked if Gauru form had gotten the same treatment as spirit ranks got, giving it a proper First Tongue term instead of sticking with the name Apocalypse werewolves use for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T18:33:42-08:00","id":815167,"title":"","content":"Gauru isn't the same as Garou, mind. Phonetically or otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T18:53:57-08:00","id":815176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815167#post815167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gauru isn't the same as Garou, mind. Phonetically or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T21:32:57-08:00","id":815243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815111#post815111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're replying to wyrdhamster's post immediately above yours, 'klaive' was never the First Tongue term for anything. It was a nonsense word when viewed through the lens of how Forsaken named other things. (There are exceptions that still exist - these are mostly Apocalypse holdovers, but they tended to have meaning that still mattered to the game.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that First Tongue name for &quot;Fetish Weapon&quot; has sense in 2ED <b>Forsaken</b>. We do not need to see <i><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">daiklave</span></span></span></i>, or any other nonsense from outside of First Tongue. But Uratha<b> are</b> hunters, and hunters use weapons - <b>a lot</b>. Especially Blood Talons and Iron Masters would use those terms most extensively. Fetish is one name for everything &quot;magical&quot; - but fetish weapons would be specific subtype in them, so spirits could agree to become &lt;Fetish Weapon&gt;, fetish smiths would know they need to make more &lt;fetish weapons&gt; etc. Uratha and spirits have their special language - seeing how &lt;Fetish Weapons&gt; are important in their culture, I would assume to be specific name for them.<br /> I'm not sure we should use Fetish also, as general term - if &quot;spirit negotiations bribes&quot; have name of <i>Gathra</i>, would not &quot;items that bound spirits&quot; would have their special name in First Tongue?<br /> <br /> As an Exalted pun, here you got what Daiklave means. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i2.photobucket.com/albums/y11/feralknights/etc/daiklave.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-24-2016, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T22:02:40-08:00","id":815253,"title":"","content":"Fetish is <i>Hithdum. </i>Weapon is <i>Kusgidu</i>. So, the First Tongue term for Fetish weapon would be <i>Hithdum kusgidu.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T22:05:48-08:00","id":815254,"title":"","content":"Klaive=/=Daiklave. There's also a limit to the amount of First Tongue names for things before you start turning people off. I don't want to have to learn a fourth language just to play a role playing game. A few terms for flavor and mood setting is fine, but there's a point where it becomes a turn off especially when we those FT words become redundant. Klaive was a redundant word for example, hence why it was dropped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T22:24:49-08:00","id":815259,"title":"","content":"I understood what you were saying wyrdhamster, thanks. I was replying to Ephsy's apparent reply to you that 'klaive' was First Tongue for fetish weapon. <br /> <br /> I guess the question to ask (and one that the writers debated) is 'why does the general grouping of fetish weapons need a special name'? Why would Uratha call fetish weapons anything other than fetish weapons. As you note, Uratha and spirits have a perfectly serviceable common language, Hithdum kusgidu works just fine. It's descriptive. It's accurate. If the Uratha need more detail, it's a fetish sword, or fetish spear, or fetish axe.<br /> <br /> Also, wyrdhamster, you're correct. Hunters use many weapons. Weapons that are functional. Weapons that aid the hunt. What *hunters* don't tend to do is use oversized decorative swords to fight against the Wyrm and Rage and scream their battle cries for Gaia in Crinos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T22:27:16-08:00","id":815261,"title":"","content":"But given First Tongue phrasing, wouldn't it be Kusgidu hithdum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T22:45:48-08:00","id":815268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815253#post815253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fetish is <i>Hithdum. </i>Weapon is <i>Kusgidu</i>. So, the First Tongue term for Fetish weapon would be <i>Hithdum kusgidu.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I just mark that <b>Charlaquin</b> answer is more than enough for me - just did not see those First Tongue terms in <b>Forsaken</b> 2ED corebook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Are there other &quot;leftovers&quot; from <b>Apocalypse</b> in <b>Forsaken</b> still?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T23:23:06-08:00","id":815281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815268#post815268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just mark that <b>Charlaquin</b> answer is more than enough for me - just did not see those First Tongue terms in <b>Forsaken</b> 2ED corebook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they are, I got them from the &quot;Doing First Tonge Translations&quot; thread. So, they're not *strictly* cannon, but they are accurate de-Grimmed Sumerian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T08:05:28-08:00","id":815460,"title":"","content":"The unihar seemed to be an artifact of Apocalypse-thought. An extension of the metis that further dissuaded play. Presumably the near-complete absence of Gaea as a known quantity has something to do with it as well, similar to the Fog of Ages in Vampire, a method to ensure you would have a different setting. I never had an Apocalypse book to really be sure but based on the art, I always thought the standard Forsaken 5 forms image was taken from the same books.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/1/1b/Shapechanger.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20101116210327\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:13:45-08:00","id":815504,"title":"","content":"Dunno about the discouraging play statement. The most epic story I ran involved a Bale Hound that passed himself as wolf-blood (Irraka) sworn to Carnala, who got female Uratha pregnant, and his Maeltinent Ancestor of a Totem took control of the eventual liter. The characters were gathered together from both Pure and Forsaken into a party from the Lodge of the Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:23:25-08:00","id":815511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815504#post815504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno about the discouraging play statement. The most epic story I ran involved a Bale Hound that passed himself as wolf-blood (Irraka) sworn to Carnala, who got female Uratha pregnant, and his Maeltinent Ancestor of a Totem took control of the eventual liter. The characters were gathered together from both Pure and Forsaken into a party from the Lodge of the Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you didn't play a unihar. Sex is one thing, but as its been described to me the metis weren't really something you were supposed to want to play, as they were burdened down by disadvantages that people mostly ended up ignoring, Similar to how Ghost Wolves are supposed to be at a disadvantage compared to members of the tribes but people want to even the playing field for them. Turning the metis into single-minded hate spirits was a good way to keep people from playing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:38:46-08:00","id":815523,"title":"","content":"Being able to just shift to Crinos whenever you like for free is apparently quite useful in WTA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T10:55:12-08:00","id":815572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815511#post815511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but you didn't play a unihar. Sex is one thing, but as its been described to me the metis weren't really something you were supposed to want to play, as they were burdened down by disadvantages that people mostly ended up ignoring, Similar to how Ghost Wolves are supposed to be at a disadvantage compared to members of the tribes but people want to even the playing field for them. Turning the metis into single-minded hate spirits was a good way to keep people from playing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A literal quote from the book is &quot;It's the final days, we cannot afford ourselves the luxury of shunning a whole breed of Gaian warriors.&quot; And if someone told you they weren't meant to be played? They were wrong. Plain and simple.<br /> <br /> The narrative themes involving metis were there to keep packs from forgetting about their given duties to Gaia when confronted with defending one's family first.<br /> <br /> The reason Unihar were there, was to re-enact Father Wolf's ban on his descendants. It was one of the things that most defined them as Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:03:37-08:00","id":815574,"title":"","content":"I'm all for extending Father Wolf's ban to his descendants, but &quot;don't fuck your family members&quot; is kind of a stupid ban.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T15:35:09-08:00","id":815724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815572#post815572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if someone told you they weren't meant to be played? They were wrong. Plain and simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Discouraged, more. Presumably if they weren't meant to be played, there would not be rules for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The narrative themes involving metis were there to keep packs from forgetting about their given duties to Gaia when confronted with defending one's family first.<br /> <br /> The reason Unihar were there, was to re-enact Father Wolf's ban on his descendants. It was one of the things that most defined them as Forsaken. </div> </div> </div>The end result for both was that werewolves shouldn't be having sex with each other. And while Father Wolf may have only been able to be killed by his progeny, werewolves had absolutely no problem killing each other. Second edition's death rage instincts seems to be the only thing that really works in regards to keeping werewolves from killing each other and it's still only active when death rage comes about. And while I've never sat in on a game, considering the history of the Garou, it seems like Garou were able to forget their duties to Gaia without their children having to do anything about it.<br /> <br /> And in both cases, werewolves still had sex with one another, so it didn't really fit as a barrier there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T16:08:15-08:00","id":815742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miriander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=814766#post814766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> W:tF 1ed felt directionless. Differences are really just a number of small things that overall add a lot to how the game is approached and played. In W:tA tribes were defined by their ideology and cultural aspects: Uktena were indians, Black Furies were feminists, Children of Gaia were human-clinging Greenpeace activists, Bone Gnawers were hobbos living on the street (I'm purposefully simplifying, please don't explode over those parallels). It carried in some way to the W:tF, differences were significant between editions, but a lot felt that new tribes are just a mix of portions of old tribes and given a motto by which they lived, while being mostly stripped from the ideological/cultural background of the predecessors. That's why Iron Masters could be percieved by some as mix of Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers or Blood Talons as mix of Fianna, Get of Fenris and Red Talons.<br /> <br /> Tribes were there on the stage of character creation, but their overall impact on the game itself wasn't big, since it was all about the pack now and not about the tribes anymore. But they were in a new game, put in a bit of a limbo of being significant and at the same time not at all.<br /> <br /> In 2ed tribes from 1ed were defined by what they hunt. It was one of those &quot;small, but big&quot; changes since suddenly when you were playing Hunter in the Darkness you weren't <i> &quot;a stealhy hunter guy who protects the wilds and who never belonged before first change, but also sometimes inhabits city and protects significant things there and also...&quot;</i>, but &quot;you are psycho killer from slasher films killing swarms of rat/spider demons&quot;. Now when in your chronicle pack of Hunters in the Darkness will appear in a territory, your players will immediately think &quot;OH MY GOLLY, @%#^ IS GOING DOWN&quot; because everybody knows why they are here and what they go for.<br /> <br /> In W:tA there were alphas as leaders of the pack, W:tF 1ed mentions those in few places (actually even at the beginning, in the tribes description) and even though from the read you are supposed to think that packs function a bit differently and alpha concept isn't as significant in W:tF, a concept still is present there and packs are made of werewolves only with some sort of leader on the hunt. Different than W:tA, but there are similarities. So while W:tF wolf-blooded aren't kinfolk, they fundamentally still function as breeding machines for furry superhumans.<br /> <br /> 2ed puts alpha term to trash and packs can consist of werewolves, wolf-blooded and even (non)ordinary humans and now everybody adds to the hunt. PCs with different tribes add to it different and wolf-blooded have some powers that werewolves never will have. Every wolf-blooded now has some distinct, werewolfy feature (Tell) that defines it. Moreover, people can become wolf-blooded due to the exposure to werewolves now, it's not only about blood lineage as previously.<br /> This is a game changer, since wolf-blooded can have very big impact on the chronicle and not be only &quot;ultimately a bit better than normal human helpers&quot;. Every wolf-blooded power is designed in a way to be potential plothook. Werewolves of which pack are murdering people on PCs territory? (None, it's a guy who became wolf-blooded after last PC action and who can now take one of the werewolf forms). There's a guy who is Pure slave that can sense hosts, every single one of them from 10 miles radius (Host-Ache tell). Forsaken must steal him to find out if they really destroyed Shartha during their last adventure.<br /> Oh and wolf-blooded and humans can perform or be part of some werewolf rituals. Suddenly capable and well organised wolf/moon cults are a thing in 2ed.<br /> <br /> Gifts. In W:tA and W:tF they worked on a scale from 1 to 5. In W:tF 2ed there's only linear progression in Moon Gifts and you get them for free, so you don't have curse of &quot;I will never get 5th!&quot;. Other Gifts (Shadow and Wolf) have Facets and they are unlocked if you have appropriate renown. They are also designed in specific way, more here:<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-...-the-forsaken/</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-...-the-forsaken/</a><br /> <br /> It's a big difference now between 1ed and 2ed, gifts are less of superpowers and more like aspects of wolf/werewolf that are in tales and trust me, they are very, very well designed. Hell, there's even a power that allows you to blow houses like a wolf from &quot;Three little pigs&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> OK, that's all kind of interesting\u200b.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Nature worth saving&quot; trope from W:tA was a bit present in W:tF 1ed, especially as I said before around Hunters in the Darkness. Now there's 0 of that. Nature works as an ally of wolf/werewolf, but is a fucking scary place and a tool of hunt. Also a place that will terrify PCs themselves (Touchstone: Call of the Wild)<br /> <br /> Harmony is another aspect in which W:tF had some influence from W:tA even though W:tA didn't have morality mechanics. Oath of the Moon was a big deal in W:tA and remained in W:tF 1ed. In 2ed it seems to be less important for morality mechanics which by the way was redesigned completely and &quot;you should not eat human flesh&quot; is more of a social and narrative problem and mechanics itself show now cannibalism as a dillemma that is there and can be counted into PCs actions. In W:tA and W:tF it really wasn't a problem, no sane player would even think about it or eat anybody bar the really extreme situations. </div> </div> </div>Sounds more like bugs than features.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T16:12:53-08:00","id":815744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815574#post815574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for extending Father Wolf's ban to his descendants, but &quot;don't fuck your family members&quot; is kind of a stupid ban.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bFrom a legal standpoint it seems like a pretty good one. I'm sorry, that was a horrible joke and I'm almost ashamed for making it. But it's been a trying day so if I didn't I'd explode, and I don't feel like cleaning up viscera from the rug.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit, yeah the first joke was reeeally bad, sorry Charlaquin. I think I need a nap and my blankey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 01-24-2016, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T16:18:27-08:00","id":815746,"title":"","content":"One thing about eating people is that Aggravated damage is <i>waaaaaay </i>less common in CoD than in cWoD, but eating people for essence is one of the few reliable ways Werewolves have of doing it. Which means it can easily be the difference between winning and losing a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T16:27:27-08:00","id":815751,"title":"","content":"Plus it's incredibly easy. Against a standard human, werewolves really dominate and eating them isn't going to be a difficult issue. But you have plenty of methods to deal with it in-game, as reactions from other packs can range from a disinterested shrug to a burning fire in their eyes as they demand the hide of the Oathbreaker. It offers more opportunities than, 'Your Harmony is now 0, hand over your character sheet.'<br /> <br /> Also I always thought the 'primary' hosts, azlu and beshilu, were inspired by the rat and spider changing breeds of Apocalypse. Not that there's much similar to them, just the choice of animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-24-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T16:46:34-08:00","id":815759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815259#post815259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What *hunters* don't tend to do is use oversized decorative swords to <b>fight against the Wyrm and Rage and scream their battle cries for Gaia</b> in Crinos.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bHere's a tip: when trying to win someone over to a game, don't mock the things they like about a game they already stated was their favorite. It's not just me you're trying to sell to, BTW. And a BIG part of what my group liked about Apocalypse was the <b>sense of purpose. </b>I'm sure you wouldn't like me to accuse the Forsaken of barking at Postal Worker spirits to stay out of their yard.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T16:51:29-08:00","id":815760,"title":"","content":"But isn't that what Apocalypse is about? Outside of the decorative part? Fighting against the wyrm? Klaives and crinos are just how they do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815759#post815759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure you wouldn't like me to accuse the Forsaken of barking at Postal Worker spirits to stay out of their yard.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it would just take a reading to show you why that was wrong. I'm surprised you didn't realize that from reading the other posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T17:10:18-08:00","id":815765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815759#post815759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHere's a tip:</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to have leaped past tips and into edges, because there's very little point in this behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> don't mock the things they like about a game </div> </div> </div>You'd have to dig rather deep and build pretty high to get mockery out of &quot;the focal characters of Werewolf: the Forsaken are not the focal characters of Werewolf: the Apocalypse.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sure you wouldn't like me to accuse the Forsaken of barking at Postal Worker spirits to stay out of their yard. </div> </div> </div>If you think this is a proportionate &quot;mockery&quot; to calling the stylistic qualities of Apocalypse's weaponry &quot;oversized [and] decorative,&quot; your problem may be bigger than economic risk-aversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T17:11:34-08:00","id":815768,"title":"","content":"Howl. They <i>howl </i> the battle cries.<br /> <br /> Also I'm pretty sure the the dude calling himself Bunyip is pretty fond of Apocalypse, y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-24-2016, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T17:13:11-08:00","id":815769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815759#post815759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHere's a tip: when trying to win someone over to a game, don't mock the things they like about a game they already stated was their favorite. It's not just me you're trying to sell to, BTW. And a BIG part of what my group liked about Apocalypse was the <b>sense of purpose. </b>I'm sure you wouldn't like me to accuse the Forsaken of barking at Postal Worker spirits to stay out of their yard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think Bunyip's trying to mock Apocalypse there. He's writing/written on a bunch of the new Werewolf: the Apocalypse books and I'm fairly sure he's a big fan of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T17:27:07-08:00","id":815777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815769#post815769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's writing/written on a bunch of the new Werewolf: the Apocalypse books</div> </div> </div> </div>He's writing/written <b>awesome stuff</b> on a bunch of the new Werewolf: the Apocalypse books, please<br /> <br /> (Sorry, had too. I love both gamelines, with their own flavor and differences, but I had to chime in and point out that those books are great. I'll see myself out)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T17:29:16-08:00","id":815778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815759#post815759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> \u200bHere's a tip: when trying to win someone over to a game, don't mock the things they like about a game they already stated was their favorite. It's not just me you're trying to sell to, BTW. And a BIG part of what my group liked about Apocalypse was the <b>sense of purpose. </b>I'm sure you wouldn't like me to accuse the Forsaken of barking at Postal Worker spirits to stay out of their yard.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies that my post came across as mocking. I love Apocalypse for being Apocalypse. I love Forsaken for being Forsaken. My intention was to highlight the differences, and the imagery I chose is a wonderful part of Apocalypse, but (IMO) not of Forsaken.<br /> <br /> But to be fair, I think this thread has moved beyond trying to sell you on Forsaken. You've repeatedly said what you like about Apocalypse, and implied if it's not in Forsaken, then you're not interested. That's fine, but we've since moved on to talking about legacy holdovers from Apocalypse to 1E Forsaken to 2E Forsaken. We've also covered terminology and different people's likes and opinions. <br /> <br /> If you're willing to be open about a different game that also happens to be about werewolves, then many people have offered suggestions and pointed you towards the developer blogs where you can get a sense of the game (since you're unwilling to take a gamble on buying the 2E pdf - which again is fine). But what you seem to want is another version of Apocalypse. Forsaken isn't that game. (But you can find many unofficial works, such as Claire's, converting various aspects of WtA into something that fits in the WtF world.)<br /> <br /> Edit: Can you assist us in advising you on Forsaken, by telling us the aspects of Apocalypse you're willing to go without? There's no universal cosmic war against the Wyrm. There's no global conspiracy like Pentex. If you really want, there's nothing stopping you from having Crinos equivalents (Gauru) with giant shiny swords howling battle cries, but that's not a key part of Forsaken.<br /> <br /> I'd love to help sell you on Forsaken, but need your help in understanding what it will take. I was of the opinion you'd already made up your mind in the negative.<br /> <br /> Double edit: Apologies I didn't address your bolded text. Forsaken have a sense of purpose, but it's both smaller (as in, not cosmic) and more intimate than fighting the Wyrm. I'd also suggest to you that Forsaken actually have a purpose they have a chance of succeeding in. They don't have a doomed purpose that they lack the tools for, and which is bound for failure. (Caveat: Individual chronicles can and will avert the Apocalypse and save Gaia. But the game line as a whole is called 'the Apocalypse' for a reason.)<br /> <br /> Triple edit: It took a re-read of nofather's post (above) to make me realise I'd mistyped a word. I meant 'oversize decorated swords' not 'decorative'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 01-25-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T17:38:37-08:00","id":815780,"title":"","content":"That comment sounded celebratory of Apocalypse, not mocking of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T19:02:44-08:00","id":815811,"title":"","content":"The way Bunyip phrased it, seemed like he was saying those parts were silly/unnecessary. I may have overreacted. Anything that comes across as &quot;Forsaken is better off without that thing that made Apocalypse AWESOME&quot; gets me upset.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, let's talk some more about Bale Hounds. Seems like the closest thing to BSDs. How much info is there on them? And how is &quot;Defend Your Territory&quot; a &quot;purpose&quot;? That's more of a &quot;personal ambition&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 01-24-2016, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T19:49:59-08:00","id":815839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815811#post815811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way Bunyip phrased it, seemed like he was saying those parts were silly/unnecessary. I may have overreacted. Anything that comes across as &amp;quot;Forsaken is better off without that thing that made Apocalypse AWESOME&amp;quot; gets me upset.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, let's talk some more about Bale Hounds. Seems like the closest thing to BSDs. How much info is there on them? And how is &amp;quot;Defend Your Territory&amp;quot; a &amp;quot;purpose&amp;quot;? That's more of a &amp;quot;personal ambition&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that it was the purpose of Father Wolf and the passing down of that responsibility is the reason the Forsaken are Forsaken, I'd say it's purpose. Purpose to live up to the names of your Mother and Father. Purpose to prove it was all worth it. For some, that may be ambitious, but it drives at the corners of your soul, and given the half-spirit nature of the Werewolfves, that's not something to take lightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T20:05:47-08:00","id":815843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815742#post815742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds more like bugs than features.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Maybe I wrote too hastly about what I feel changed about morality. I meant to say - in W:tA and partly in W:tF 1ed you didn't have a reason to break the Oath of the Moon or to do things &quot;wrong&quot;. GM would have to really raiload you to have some moral dilemma since everything was pretty one dimensional &quot;don't eat humans unless you want to end up dancing the black spiral&quot;, &quot;respect hierarchy you a-hole&quot;. <br /> <br /> Now your characters have more dimension. Disregarding the fact that every PC has to choose at the level of character creation 1 thing that ties it to the spiritual side and 1 thing that ties it to the human/physical side as well as how he behaves off and on the hunt, now players have morality mechanics that actively influence them and determine a number of things, among others how easily it is to change shape for them or how long and strong they can resist Death Rage and if they are more suspectible to it or not. Some merits also require you to maintain certain Harmony level. <br /> <br /> As a result some &quot;sins&quot; against Harmony seem to be a fair exchange over the boon they give you.<br /> <br /> As I said, in W:tA and W:tF 1ed nobody had a reason to eat anyone. Now eating another werewolf might be a way to make aggrevated damage and replenish essence in battle by substantial amount and it really makes a difference, especially against stronger opponents. Same with killing someone with silver weapons - you actually feel like the risk is worth it since again, there's not many other ways in which you can do aggrevated damage to werewolf (compared to previous editions). <br /> <br /> If you feel your PC becomes too much inhuman spirit more and more alien to the world, you could choose to say &quot;Enough, I don't want to hunt! I don't care what Luna wants! I can't live like this, I need time...I'm going to my ex&quot; and effectively break the Oath of the Moon and one of the few sacred, fundamental things about werewolf life (have to hunt). Now though that change might be beneficial for you - you move on the Harmony scale towards Flesh, and meeting again with your old love effectively makes you more of a balanced individual, not so prone to rage constantly and having more control over when you shift to other form. Mechanics directly supports narration.<br /> <br /> Sure, you did wrong thing in the eyes of other characters. It's up to the NPCs, game world and other PCs to judge this deedm but now the problem isn't as one dimensional as before. In old editions a PC would be &quot;Luna's traitor&quot; and objectively evil. Now there's a clear reason for his behaviour - actually regaining a grip on his life - and everybody should understand that, especially other players since the same mechanics affects them. I don't see lots of &quot;how could youuuuuuu&quot; being shouted now at the gaming table even though choices might be even more dramatic. Suddenly a Lune hunting a packmate to punish him might not be right...<br /> <br /> %%%<br /> <br /> Things with nature...well, depends on what you like. You definietly could go for ecological themes too in W:tF 2ed if you wish so, but by default you don't have to. You aren't there to protect nature, but to protect your territory. You aren't nature's warrior, you are a hunter that is part of nature. You see, accents are laid out differently. <br /> <br /> Example: Nature's Gift in W:tF 1ed. There's talking with animals, there's controlling plant growth and suggestion that you can make a treehouse out of it (like elves), a power that makes you &quot;one with the forest&quot;, sensing surrounding etc.<br /> <br /> You have this shamanic and &quot;wise native&quot; and nature-loving vibes from it.<br /> <br /> Compare it to W:tF 2ed: a power that compells a prey to enter the wild, lures it into the forest. A power that makes prey unable to escape the territory, go around the forest and always end up in the same place. A power that makes predator(s) be part of your pack, so you can run with wolves or have bloody grizzly bears aid you with your attack on police station. <br /> <br /> Both editions have a power that allows you to control some animal or beast. <br /> <br /> See the difference? In 2ed everything was about being a predator. Nature works in that way - as predatory, mysterious, savage, scary. Sure, it might be your home and something really precious to you and you can certainly put emphasis on it in your game - but it's up to you. As default, 2ed gives nature teeth - and it's fitting, since the wolf resides in the forest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T20:14:08-08:00","id":815846,"title":"","content":"I've always loved Apocalypse, but it's almost always been heavy with metaplot, dogmatically oppressive cultures, and plain disinterest in actual real-world mythology. This was a lingering feature of CWoD games, so it's not a specific complaint, but the Garou were probably the biggest departure of any of those monsters.<br /> <br /> Not that 1e Forsaken were much better, but they were measured against their fellow inhabitants, weren't thrust into a weirdly racialized society of eco-warriors, and weren't under the thumb of the elders to fight a very real and demonstrable threat to all of existence.<br /> <br /> Now 2e Forsaken are bloody fucking <i>werewolves</i>. They lose their shit on the regular, they hunt because they have to, and they live in fear of becoming lost to their extremes. They aren't furry superheroes, they aren't insular spirit cops treading lightly between worlds, they are primal rage monsters barely contained by the Flesh and basically trying to keep the rest of the world from becoming as messed up as themselves. They do find some beauty and revel in their existence and purpose, and the human left in them creates culture and ritual, but it's not the heart of their existence as the Garou experience it.<br /> <br /> Given a choice, I would go for the Uratha over the Garou. The Garou are zealots, unmoored from human concerns, and largely unconcerned by the violence they unleash. The Forsaken live in a grayer world, with fewer allies and less clear purpose, and don't have some merciful and loving goddess to forgive their transgressions, but only the company of demanding Totems and the warped unfortunates with Wolf's blood. There's more innocents in the path of the Forsaken, forcing players into more complex solutions or much riskier violence, or both. The evil in the world isn't at the urging of an over-arching cosmic being, but the natural tendencies of humans and spirits going unchecked. At its heart, these obstacles ground Forsaken in more relatable dilemmas than which Wyrm-creature to hunt down or which hidebound elder needs to be appeased. They can still resort to violence and carnage, but it comes at a cost the militant Garou rarely consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T20:21:12-08:00","id":815851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815811#post815811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSo, let's talk some more about Bale Hounds. Seems like the closest thing to BSDs. How much info is there on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're only really expanded upon in the Blasphemies book. Myself and other fans are eager to see their second edition interpretation.<br /> <br /> In first edition, they exist in a few different forms. They range from werewolves who have made deals with the Maeljin or their lieutenants the Maeltinet, which sort of act like demon pacts since the Maeljin are comparable to demon lords. Blasphemies offers a few more options, with you letting you choose which one is more appropriate for your game. You have the Lodge, which acts probably the most like the 'its just a pact' thing, where outside of your dealings with the Maeljin you are basically a normal werewolf in a tribe going about your business. Then you have the Dark Pantheism option, which has them as rabid servants of the Maeljin, either sworn to one or a group of them. And my favorite option, though I use all of them, was the Ninth Tribe, which has them serving one of the Firstborn and existing as another tribe entirely, keeping their affiliation secret.<br /> <br /> Each of the Maeljin were associated with one of the 9 sins of werewolves. Lust, Envy, Pride, Wrath, Greed, Gluttony, Sloth, Violence and Deceit. Second edition seems to have opened this up so that there's more than first edition's 9. The Dark Pantheism option seemed to take the most violent angle with them, as they are out there tearing open Wounds and doing evil. The other options had them more as corruptors, getting others to succumb to the sins of their masters. In exchange, it is rumored they would become Maeladar, more spiritually in touch with their Maeljin master as an immortal spirit aspect of them.<br /> <br /> I suppose the term Maeljin would be another artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-24-2016, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T20:34:22-08:00","id":815857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815811#post815811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way Bunyip phrased it, seemed like he was saying those parts were silly/unnecessary. I may have overreacted. Anything that comes across as &quot;Forsaken is better off without that thing that made Apocalypse AWESOME&quot; gets me upset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't meant to be upsetting with this, but... Forsaken kinda is better off without the things that made Apocalypse awesome. Not because those things aren't awesome. They are. But Apocalypse already exists, and it already does those things better than Forsaken can. Forsaken is never going to beat Apocalypse at its own game, and when it tries, you end up with early Forsaken 1e. What 2e did was said, &quot;let's let Apocalypse be the game you play for the things that made Apocalypse awesome, and make Forsaken into the game you play for the things that make Forsaken awesome.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-25-2016, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T20:51:49-08:00","id":815871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815851#post815851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're only really expanded upon in the Blasphemies book. Myself and other fans are eager to see their second edition interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bSeconded.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T21:02:15-08:00","id":815879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815857#post815857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't meant to be upsetting with this, but... Forsaken kinda is better off without the things that made Apocalypse awesome. Not because those things aren't awesome. They are. But Apocalypse already exists, and it already does those things better than Forsaken can. Forsaken is never going to beat Apocalypse at its own game, and when it tries, you end up with early Forsaken 1e. What 2e did was said, &quot;let's let Apocalypse be the game you play for the things that made Appcalypse awesome, and make Forsaken into the game you play for the things that make Forsaken awesome.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>'Zactly. If you want to play Apocalypse, it's right there, and it's coming back to life all over again, Ye shall want for nothing! But, if a player wants to explore themes like the loss of control, body and spirit horror, and primal terror, that is something that is done better with Forsaken. Both give you violence, power trips, and weird animism, but one gives you moral clarity and cosmic evil while the other gives you grey areas and bloody-handed amnesia. Those are for different players and different moods.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T21:48:36-08:00","id":815894,"title":"","content":"Apocalypse is an adventure game, Forsaken is a horror game. It really boils down to that. Prior to Exalted 1e if you wanted a WW game of epic heros and glorious battles Apocalypse was your go to game, but while it featured werewolves it really wasn't about being werewolves, it was about being part of a warrior culture. Forsaken 2e concentrates on what it's like to be a werewolf, a hunter rather than a warrior. Between the two, even though Forsaken is a horror game it's less pessimistic in tone. I prefer that. I liked Apocalypse (I even still have Freak Legion on the shelf next to me) but it was very much a product of the 90's and my tastes have changed since then.<br /> <br /> They're just two very different experiences, highlighted most strongly by the fact that Apocalypse encourages players to stay away from their mortal family while to one of the Forsaken your family is often part of your pack and is integral to your existence. Forsaken feels a lot more personal in scope and it also seems to give the players a bit more agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 01-25-2016, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T21:50:26-08:00","id":815895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815811#post815811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything that comes across as &quot;Forsaken is better off without that thing that made Apocalypse AWESOME&quot; gets me upset.</div> </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't make you upset.<br /> Not anymore than saying &quot;Zelda is better off without the thing that made <i>Mario </i>AWESOME.&quot; Or maybe a better analogy is &quot;Castlevania is better off not being Metroid,&quot; because that analogy is closer.<br /> <br /> Different games made by the same company using many of the same base elements. And they're better off having their own unique flavors, their own twists, their own turns.<br /> <br /> The thing is, you come here expecting that this new edition should be closer to Apocalypse under the assumption that since Apocalypse worked in your eyes, Forsaken should be like the original game that made werewolves a solid RPG.<br /> <br /> The truth of the very matter is that Forsaken 2e is a very different game from Apocalypse... and it's still a world different from Forsaken 1e, it's immediate predacessor!<br /> <br /> The things that made Apocalypse good wouldn't work for Forsaken due to the very nature of Forsaken being so utterly different than Apocalypse. They're practically in different genres all together.<br /> <br /> You might as well be say inserting Chucky the killer doll in Toy Story 2, Mister Freeze from Batman and Robin into the Dark Knight Returns, Scooby Doo in Air Bud, or even Tarzan into Planet of the Apes and Gundams into WALL-E.<br /> Each of those elements above has something tangentally related to the other, and all of them are great characters in their own rights in their own worlds. Their inclusions however would massively warp the very nature of another setting if they were ever seriously added into them. And this is the situation that adding in elements of Apocalypse would create.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, yes. &quot;Forsaken is better off without the thing that made Apocalypse AWESOME&quot;. In much the same way the different Batman movies are better off without elements from a different film continuity. Seriously, Adam West Batman would not be good for modern Dark Knight Films or the Arkham games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 01-25-2016, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T22:33:18-08:00","id":815905,"title":"","content":"Looking at Forsaken as Apocalypse 2.0 isn't going to leave you satisfied, it isn't and it doesn't attempt to be. It doesn't really make sense for it to try and be &quot;similar but different&quot;, especially when an updated version of Apocalypse is currently available. Most players I know would get pretty irritated at being sold the same game in slightly different packaging. If you like the rule set for Forsaken better but the Apocalypse setting better then take a look at the conversion guide on DTRPG, that might be helpful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T23:25:57-08:00","id":815925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815905#post815905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at Forsaken as Apocalypse 2.0 isn't going to leave you satisfied, it isn't and it doesn't attempt to be. It doesn't really make sense for it to try and be &quot;similar but different&quot;, especially when an updated version of Apocalypse is currently available. Most players I know would get pretty irritated at being sold the same game in slightly different packaging. If you like the rule set for Forsaken better but the Apocalypse setting better then take a look at the conversion guide on DTRPG, that might be helpful</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that's probably what I'll do, and that's assuming I can even get my group to play CofD at all, since most of them prefer CWoD. Seriously, we've only had one game last more a few sessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T23:29:19-08:00","id":815926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815857#post815857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't meant to be upsetting with this, but... Forsaken kinda is better off without the things that made Apocalypse awesome. Not because those things aren't awesome. They are. But Apocalypse already exists, and it already does those things better than Forsaken can. Forsaken is never going to beat Apocalypse at its own game, and when it tries, you end up with early Forsaken 1e. What 2e did was said, &quot;let's let Apocalypse be the game you play for the things that made Apocalypse awesome, and make Forsaken into the game you play for the things that make Forsaken awesome.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815905#post815905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at Forsaken as Apocalypse 2.0 isn't going to leave you satisfied, it isn't and it doesn't attempt to be. It doesn't really make sense for it to try and be &quot;similar but different&quot;, especially when an updated version of Apocalypse is currently available. Most players I know would get pretty irritated at being sold the same game in slightly different packaging. If you like the rule set for Forsaken better but the Apocalypse setting better then take a look at the conversion guide on DTRPG, that might be helpful</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These two posts sum it up perfectly, I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T23:58:27-08:00","id":815933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815851#post815851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each of the Maeljin were associated with one of the 9 sins of werewolves. Lust, Envy, Pride, Wrath, Greed, Gluttony, Sloth, Violence and Deceit. Second edition seems to have opened this up so that there's more than first edition's 9. The Dark Pantheism option seemed to take the most violent angle with them, as they are out there tearing open Wounds and doing evil. The other options had them more as corruptors, getting others to succumb to the sins of their masters. In exchange, it is rumored they would become Maeladar, more spiritually in touch with their Maeljin master as an immortal spirit aspect of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the day to day basis, Bale Hounds are working with Souless Wolf Totem, that is weird mockery of normal Forsaken and Pure Firstborns - but he states he is their &quot;family member&quot;. I only point that I proposed fan idea in that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">Souless Wolf is what left of Father Wolf </a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">corrupted</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\"> by Maeljins</a> - it makes really interesting dynamic in that the most &quot;true&quot; Forsaken and Pure can be seduced in to Bale Hounds by &quot;following your parents footsteps&quot;... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T00:17:09-08:00","id":815936,"title":"","content":"One of the Maeltinet already claims to be the reanimated remains of Father Wolf. Soulless Wolf claims to be one of the Firstborn, one whose name was stricken for doing something unspeakable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T06:12:43-08:00","id":816043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815933#post815933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the day to day basis, Bale Hounds are working with Souless Wolf Totem, that is weird mockery of normal Forsaken and Pure Firstborns - but he states he is their &quot;family member&quot;. I only point that I proposed fan idea in that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">Souless Wolf is what left of Father Wolf </a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">corrupted</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\"> by Maeljins</a> - it makes really interesting dynamic in that the most &quot;true&quot; Forsaken and Pure can be seduced in to Bale Hounds by &quot;following your parents footsteps&quot;... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's certainly <i>one</i> option, as presented in <b>Blasphemies</b>. What they'll be like in 2e is anybody's guess other than probably Stew. I have a feeling he's got some ideas.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm definitely looking forward to seeing what 2e has in store for the Bale Hounds (and of course, hopefully writing on that project!).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T08:05:30-08:00","id":816115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=815925#post815925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI think that's probably what I'll do, and that's assuming I can even get my group to play CofD at all, since most of them prefer CWoD. Seriously, we've only had one game last more a few sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very much the same uphill battle that a person who plays one edition of D&amp;D within a specific setting made by the publishers wants to convince his gaming buddies to try a new edition that has a different setting. I.E. <br /> <br /> 3.5 Eberron and Forgotten Realms transfering over to Pathfinder Golarion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T22:53:43-08:00","id":816687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=816115#post816115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's very much the same uphill battle that a person who plays one edition of D&amp;D within a specific setting made by the publishers wants to convince his gaming buddies to try a new edition that has a different setting. I.E.<br /> <br /> 3.5 Eberron and Forgotten Realms transfering over to Pathfinder Golarion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty weak example since you can play Eberron and Forgotten Realms in Pathfinder, and Golarion is already basically Forgetten Realms + Even more &quot;everything but the kitchen sink&quot;. Since.... well it's only a slightly touched up version of 3.5e... While WTF and WTA function on completely different themes and styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T23:12:15-08:00","id":816692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=816687#post816687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a pretty weak example since you can play Eberron and Forgotten Realms in Pathfinder, and Golarion is already basically Forgetten Realms + Even more &quot;everything but the kitchen sink&quot;. Since.... well it's only a slightly touched up version of 3.5e... While WTF and WTA function on completely different themes and styles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was the closest I could think of since ultimately, NWoD and CWoD used the same basic rule ideas with changes thrown in, granted the Storyteller and Storytelling system have major changes between them.<br /> <br /> No, what I was talking about was more the &quot;flavor&quot; of the settings being fundamentally different.<br /> <br /> There's probably a better example that I am just not thinking of...<br /> <br /> Maybe Greyhawk or Dragonlance and Eberron with Advanced and 3.5/4e instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T23:22:51-08:00","id":816699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/813506-sell-an-apocalypse-fan-on-forsaken-or-w-tf-wtf?p=816692#post816692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It was the closest I could think of since ultimately, NWoD and CWoD used the same basic rule ideas with changes thrown in, granted the Storyteller and Storytelling system have major changes between them.<br /> <br /> No, what I was talking about was more the &quot;flavor&quot; of the settings being fundamentally different.<br /> <br /> There's probably a better example that I am just not thinking of...<br /> <br /> Maybe Greyhawk or Dragonlance and Eberron with Advanced and 3.5/4e instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Sun and Eberron maybe? Magic inflicted post-apocalyptic wasteland vs. Pulp Manapunk (even if it is just steampunk with magic paint rather than proper manapunk...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}